## Spatial, temporal, textural, transition, pressure/release, and recurrence maps

- **Spatial:** juniper is a close spherical cap; ginger is a wet diagonal; violet is a middle tailored shell; differentiated cedar is a faceted back wall; vetiver is the downward root axis; mineral air occupies the gaps.
- **Temporal:** opening 0–5 min berry/bergamot pressure; top 5–30 min wet ginger/basil seam; heart 30–120 min violet cloth and mineral air; late heart 2–6 h cedar facets; drydown 6–24 h root-dry juniper echo. **NOT TESTED**.
- **Nineteen textures:** polished; waxed; wet-cut; cool-berry; crisp; fatty; fibrous; tailored-cloth; leafy; metallic; bitter; humid; mineral; pencil-dry; smoky-dry; rooty; creamy-yielding; textile; slow.
- **Pressure/release:** juniper presses outward; ginger punctures; green-violet cloth contains; air releases; cedar facets resist; sandal yields; vetiver drains.
- **Ten links:** (1) bergamot→juniper, (2) juniper→ginger, (3) ginger→basil, (4) basil→violet, (5) violet→mineral air, (6) air→Virginia cedar, (7) cedar→Clearwood, (8) wood→sandal yield, (9) sandal→vetiver, (10) terpinyl→juniper recurrence.

