## Future mixing order

If later authorized: (1) benzoate/salicylate and root materials; (2) three cedars/Clearwood and sandal; (3) ionone cloth; (4) floral/mineral air; (5) green stitches; (6) ginger; (7) juniper and bergamot last; (8) alcohol phase. Record stock labels, masses, order, clarity, temperature, and losses. **No physical compounding is authorized.**

## Controlled blinded test plan

Compare stock-corrected L'Homme V6 and LH-04 as independently prepared, constant-total 6,000 uL concentrates with matched final concentration and carrier composition. Use two independently prepared complete sets, anonymous codes, AB/BA counterbalance, equal substrates, and free description before scoring at 0, 5, 30, 120 minutes, 6 hours, and 24 hours.

**Juniper dose-isolation triangle:** prepare three independent LH-04 arms: `juniper omission` = 0 uL Juniper stock + 100 uL DPG; `juniper low` = 50 uL Juniper 10% DPG + 50 uL DPG; `juniper main` = 100 uL Juniper 10% DPG + 0 uL in-slot DPG. All formula concentrates remain 6,000 uL. To make the carrier vector exact, add 10 uL DPG outside the main concentrate and add 10 uL of a labeled 50% v/v DPG-in-ethanol completion stock outside the low concentrate; omission needs no outside DPG. Prepare that completion stock from 100 uL DPG + 100 uL ethanol, and adjust final ethanol so every finished sample remains equal. Thus each arm has 100 uL DPG while the isolated nominal-active Juniper doses are 0/5/10 uL, and every measured aliquot is at least 10 uL. Randomize codes within each replicate; a null result tests only these doses and this protocol.

Score separately: opening pleasure, juniper clarity, ginger cut, violet tailoring, juniper recurrence, cedar differentiation, root dryness, transition pleasure, drydown pleasure, overall liking, re-smell desire, muddiness, gin, cleaner, fougère, shower-gel, and harsh-terpene defects. A null recurrence rating rejects the claimed mechanism; it is not evidence of subtle complexity.

